      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Quiz: Which of the following media query syntax is correct?"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Tap an option below to answer:"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "css",
      "content": "body {\n    @media (min-width: 600px) {\n        background-color: lightblue;\n    }\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "content": "Incorrect, give it another shot!"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The CSS rulesets must be defined inside the @media keyword, not outside."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The CSS rulesets must be defined inside the @media keyword, not outside."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "css",
      "content": "media (min-width: 600px) {\n    body {\n        background-color: lightblue;\n    }\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "content": "Incorrect, give it another shot!"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Using only media is incorrect as it's missing the @ symbol. Instead, the correct keyword is @media."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Using only media is incorrect as it's missing the @ symbol. Instead, the correct keyword is @media."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "css",
      "content": "@media (min-width: 600px) {\n    body {\n        background-color: lightblue;\n    }\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "content": "Correct Answer!"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The @media keyword indicates the start of a media query, followed by the CSS rulesets that define the changes to take place in the given condition."
    },
    {
